  "question": {
    "text": "The decreasing order of bond angles in $\\mathrm{BF}_3, \\mathrm{NH}_3, \\mathrm{PF}_3$ and $\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}$is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YDFEH",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}>\\mathrm{BF}_3>\\mathrm{NH}_3>\\mathrm{PF}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "O7kFD",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{BF}_3>\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}>\\mathrm{PF}_3>\\mathrm{NH}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RF6EU",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{BF}_3>\\mathrm{NH}_3>\\mathrm{PF}_3>\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WPPSP",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}>\\mathrm{NH}_3>\\mathrm{PF}_3>\\mathrm{BF}_3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/apA7RcGev549JDZF5zkFnxX7cOMl0l60di6NxjlNwb8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\text { B is } s p^2 \\text {, Bond angle }=120^{\\circ}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/sUEElVHjkmmBgfPx10O6BQ5mYX_Z78npKoybx3Hl188.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\mathrm{N} \\text { is } s p^3 \\text { with } 1 ~l p, \\text { Bond angle }=107^{\\circ}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pQYkjmJVY2MWHJoh9-olMeLnfG3TelEUnVxyMTdMnNs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\mathrm{P} \\text { is } s p^3 \\text { with } 1 ~l p$ , when central atom\nsize $\\uparrow$, bond angle $\\downarrow, \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{NH}_3>\\mathrm{PF}_3$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Bh_rSdCqhuO0VlYRacDiHjEE2BynVHF1yzP5JpM83Ho.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\mathrm{I}$ is $s p^3 d$ (linear), Bond angle $=180^{\\circ}$\n$\\therefore \\quad$ Decreasing order of bond angle\n$\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}>\\mathrm{BF}_3>\\mathrm{NH}_3>\\mathrm{PF}_3$",
    "image": null
  },
